Review probes (PR #314, Review R): files and packages. A required file
with no script extension (none, .txt) runs as JavaScript under require, so
it is analyzed as JavaScript, and one that does not lex is unverified. An
installed link is checked before a declaration is trusted: a link into a
node is a violation even for a declared registry dependency, and a link to
shared project code is never followed (unverified). Undeclared installed
code is unverified. The remaining probes are resolution controls that
already held: export *, #imports, tsconfig paths and extends, exports
arrays and conditions, .mts/.cts, JSX, index files and letter case.
